      "updated": 1789746203980,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Patterns for working with test doubles (usually just call these all \"mocks\"):\n    - Use a test double as a \"Dummy\" \n        - just used so you don't get a null reference exception, doesn't impact the test.\n   - Use a test double as a \"Stub\"\n        - \"State based testing\" - set up a test double such that the state of the SUT will change based on correct interactions,.\n        - we know the bonus calculator is being properly interacted with because the \"stubbed\" value is added to our balance.\n        - The test double is programmed to return a fixed value usually based certain inputs.\n    - Use a test double as a \"Mock\"\n        - \"Mockist\" or \"London School\" of testing.\n        - Records all interactions, and allows you to verify them\n          as part of the assertion of your test.\n    - Use a test double that is a \"Fake\"\n        - Something that represents a 'real' thing that is outside your application code.\n        - Databases are a common example\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Patterns for working with test doubles (usually just call these all \"mocks\"):\n    - Use a test double as a \"Dummy\" \n        - just used so you don't get a null reference exception, doesn't impact the test.\n   - Use a test double as a \"Stub\"\n        - \"State based testing\" - set up a test double such that the state of the SUT will change based on correct interactions,.\n        - we know the bonus calculator is being properly interacted with because the \"stubbed\" value is added to our balance.\n        - The test double is programmed to return a fixed value usually based certain inputs.\n    - Use a test double as a \"Mock\"\n        - \"Mockist\" or \"London School\" of testing.\n        - Records all interactions, and allows you to verify them\n          as part of the assertion of your test.\n    - Use a test double that is a \"Fake\"\n        - Something that represents a 'real' thing that is outside your application code.\n        - Databases are a common example\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
